Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; FIXME(remove-when-fixed): Wine's default "Light" visual theme.
;
; What is broken (seen with Wine 10.0 and 11.0): with the theme active, the
; themed EDIT control's WM_NCPAINT fills the whole control, client area
; included. Apps that draw an edit control's text themselves and then send
; WM_NCPAINT (the Clarion runtime does, for every ENTRY field) get the text
; painted over: typed characters are invisible although they are stored.
;
; Why this is safe: disabling the theme gives the classic look Wine used by
; default before 9.0; nothing functional depends on it.
;
; How to remove: once the upstream fix is in the pinned Wine release (see
; docs/wine-patches.md for the bug link), delete this file and check that
; typed text shows up in the app's input fields.

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\ThemeManager]
"ThemeActive"="0"
